1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,977
Dust and

2
00:00:02,060 --> 00:00:09,060
Cash

3
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:31,520
I love you, I love you.

4
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:11,657
Thank

5
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:13,057
you

6
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:20,140
so

7
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:23,559
much for watching.

8
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:33,777
After rescuing the Gotsumon from
the Digimon Emperor's prison,

9
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:36,860
Gatomon saw this strange
control spire. Meanwhile,

10
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:41,197
the Emperor and his Vegiemon slaves
captured Gabumon in a village of Gazimon.

11
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:43,677
Red Vegiemon threw Gabumon into the river,

12
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:46,557
but he was still able to call
Matt and the rest of us for help.

13
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:49,597
We rescued the Gazimon by
pretending to be prisoners,

14
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:50,957
but the Vegiemon found us again.

15
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:53,800
When Red Vegiemon cracked
the control spire,

16
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:56,729
Gabumon was able to
digivolve to Garurumon.

17
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:59,437
That spire was the key to
the Digimon Emperor's power

18
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:02,520
and our new mission is to
destroy the rest of them.

19
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:07,620
Dark Tower, house!

20
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:18,150
That's it!

21
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:20,480
Where it is, it's cold.

22
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:23,700
Ah, leave me alone!

23
00:02:25,420 --> 00:02:26,250
Get up!

24
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:28,760
Dog! Dog!

25
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:31,600
Hey, quit it!

26
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:34,322
They're all tired and need rest.

27
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:37,537
Maybe someone should use this
whip on you, you big bully.

28
00:02:37,620 --> 00:02:40,597
Number one, don't ever talk
to me without calling me sir.

29
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:42,860
Number two, don't ever talk to me!

30
00:02:43,020 --> 00:02:47,357
Whoever among you can defeat this creature
will receive a special prize package.

31
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:49,377
The rest will get some
lovely parting gifts.

32
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:51,284
So who is up for the challenge?

33
00:02:57,460 --> 00:02:59,340
I know all about Gizamon.

34
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,917
They're amphibian
Digimon with webbed feet.

35
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,417
Their fins cut through
the water like knives.

36
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:06,040
They won't attack me.

37
00:03:13,140 --> 00:03:15,360
That was way too easy.

38
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:17,597
Yeah, they've defeated him, Master.

39
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:19,157
Now tell them what they've won.

40
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,070
Right.

41
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:29,380
Here's your reward.

42
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:32,200
You all have the honor of being my slaves.

43
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:35,032
Now get back to work building the prison.

44
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:38,760
Move it, Wormon.

45
00:03:39,020 --> 00:03:41,057
I want you to make me a hot chocolate.

46
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:42,360
What about Gormomon?

47
00:03:42,660 --> 00:03:43,580
Let him freeze.

48
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:50,280
I've just got to climb
up this little hill.

49
00:03:58,240 --> 00:04:01,880
Okay, maybe it's not such
a little hill after all.

50
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:03,720
What's that?

51
00:04:09,900 --> 00:04:11,800
Uh, uh, uh, uh, Joe!

52
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:15,820
Go, Mammon!

53
00:04:16,060 --> 00:04:17,037
So how about it, guys?

54
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:18,977
Are you all ready for that
big anatomy test today?

55
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:20,997
Yeah, I spent the whole
night looking in the mirror.

56
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:22,197
How about you, Joe?

57
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:24,977
Uh, I just remembered that I
forgot to remember something.

58
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:25,890
I gotta go.

59
00:04:29,580 --> 00:04:30,410
Hey, Cody!

60
00:04:31,260 --> 00:04:33,140
Oh, hi, Davis. What's up?

61
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:34,630
What's up?

62
00:04:34,713 --> 00:04:35,543
Are you crazy?

63
00:04:35,626 --> 00:04:36,456
Where are you going?

64
00:04:36,539 --> 00:04:37,369
I'm going home.

65
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:39,577
I've got kendo practice this afternoon.

66
00:04:39,660 --> 00:04:41,020
What? Practice later!

67
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:42,868
The digi world's in danger!

68
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:45,777
Sorry, Davis, but my
grandfather is the teacher,

69
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:48,837
and he would be very disappointed
if I missed a lesson.

70
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:49,750
See ya.

71
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:52,857
Yeah, but...

72
00:04:52,940 --> 00:04:54,528
What's the matter with you?

73
00:04:54,940 --> 00:04:55,780
Kari, great!

74
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,357
I'm going to the computer room.

75
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:58,457
Why don't you come with me?

76
00:04:58,540 --> 00:05:00,140
Sure, let's go. Really?

77
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:03,517
You and I together all alone
in the dangerous digital world?

78
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:06,071
Finally, it'll be like my dream come true.

79
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:07,380
Excuse me?

80
00:05:07,540 --> 00:05:09,128
I said I'm studying French.

81
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:10,110
Parlez-vous?

82
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:17,500
I just can't win.

83
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:19,480
What's going on?

84
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:21,677
We just got a message
from the digital world.

85
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:23,677
It's a distress call
from one of the Digimon.

86
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:24,590
Who?

87
00:05:24,673 --> 00:05:25,652
I'm not really sure yet.

88
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:27,310
I've got it.

89
00:05:27,540 --> 00:05:31,697
The signal is coming from one of the black
areas controlled by the Digimon Emperor.

90
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:34,217
And it's a lot further than
any area we've been to.

91
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:37,241
Well, this should add to
our frequent flyer miles.

92
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:40,317
According to this map, the Emperor's
area is getting a lot bigger.

93
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,617
I bet his ego is, too.

94
00:05:41,700 --> 00:05:45,077
It won't be long before he
controls the entire digital world.

95
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:47,454
Then every single Digimon is in danger.

96
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,317
All right, I've had enough of this clown.

97
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:53,277
Let's all head to the digital world.

98
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:55,617
But we have to wait for Cody to get here.

99
00:05:55,700 --> 00:05:56,740
He's not coming.

100
00:05:57,280 --> 00:05:58,221
What's he doing?

101
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:00,300
He says he has kendo practice.

102
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:02,388
One question, what's kendo?

103
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:05,712
What did you hit me for?

104
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:07,841
You wanted to know what Kendo is.

105
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:25,638
Let's take a break.

106
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:27,797
What's the matter with you today, Cody?

107
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:30,457
You just don't seem to
be concentrating enough.

108
00:06:30,540 --> 00:06:32,180
I'm sorry, Grandfather.

109
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:35,337
You haven't lost interest in
the martial arts, have you?

110
00:06:35,420 --> 00:06:37,357
Or hanging out with your old grandpa?

111
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:38,270
Of course not.

112
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:39,460
I can read faces.

113
00:06:40,280 --> 00:06:44,077
Your expression tells me that
something is troubling you deep inside.

114
00:06:44,160 --> 00:06:46,817
Your father acted the same
way when he was a boy.

115
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:49,477
I have been to many lands
and met many people.

116
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:53,442
And in all my travels, I have found
only one thing I can count on.

117
00:06:53,980 --> 00:06:55,460
Prune juice! Ha!

118
00:06:56,940 --> 00:06:58,740
Yep, take two big glasses.

119
00:06:58,900 --> 00:06:59,817
You'll be fine.

120
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:04,200
You want some? No thanks.

121
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:07,497
I'm afraid that my problem is
even too big for prune juice.

122
00:07:07,580 --> 00:07:08,410
Hmm?

123
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:11,517
There are others who are
counting on me to do something,

124
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:13,297
and I'm afraid I might let them down.

125
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:14,792
I once told your father,

126
00:07:15,220 --> 00:07:19,279
people will rely on you only to the
extent that you rely on yourself.

127
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:22,325
Try your hardest and you
won't let anyone down.

128
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:25,150
Right.

129
00:07:25,233 --> 00:07:26,497
I've got to go, Grandpa.

130
00:07:26,580 --> 00:07:27,874
Thanks for the advice.

131
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:29,590
See ya.

132
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:33,620
No problem is too big for prune juice.

133
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:39,290
Oh, boy!

134
00:07:39,373 --> 00:07:40,757
I knew Cody would show up!

135
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:41,997
It's not Cody, okay?

136
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:43,198
Now everybody hide!

137
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:48,460
It's Joe!

138
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:50,760
Hi, guys.

139
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:53,430
Wow,

140
00:07:53,513 --> 00:07:54,737
even though Tai told me about it,

141
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:57,317
it's still strange seeing the
Digimon here in the real world.

142
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,737
This is Joe, our old
friend we told you about.

143
00:07:59,820 --> 00:08:01,420
Oh, the doctor.

144
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:02,998
That's really cool.

145
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:06,057
Would you mind taking a
look at my tonsils for me?

146
00:08:06,140 --> 00:08:07,757
Joe, this is Davis and Yoli.

147
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:09,605
Joe's not really a doctor yet.

148
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:10,977
I'm glad you're here.

149
00:08:11,060 --> 00:08:13,117
We got a distress call from the DigiWorld.

150
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:14,030
I know.

151
00:08:14,113 --> 00:08:14,943
It's from GoMama.

152
00:08:15,026 --> 00:08:16,137
So your DigiVice was triggered, too?

153
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:18,020
That's why you came. Candy!

154
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:21,952
Hey, these are supplies for an emergency.

155
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:25,737
Do you plan on coming to the
Digital World with us, Joe?

156
00:08:25,820 --> 00:08:27,585
We could really use your help.

157
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:28,950
Absolutely.

158
00:08:29,033 --> 00:08:30,009
I'm worried about Gomamon.

159
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:33,302
These are the digivices
of the new Digidestined.

160
00:08:33,420 --> 00:08:36,717
They're the only things that can
open the gate to the digital world.

161
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:38,697
Yeah, Izzy gave me a heads up about them.

162
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:43,177
And he also told me all about this jerk
that calls himself the Digimon Emperor.

163
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:45,084
All right, let's open the gate.

164
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:46,010
Right.

165
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:48,400
What about me?

166
00:08:55,073 --> 00:08:55,997
You're going to have to forgive him.

167
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:57,080
He's hyperactive.

168
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:59,282
Hey, everybody, the gate's open.

169
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:02,520
All right, come on, let's go!

170
00:09:17,020 --> 00:09:18,900
Great, I hate the cold.

171
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:21,320
Kari, are you okay? Mm-hmm.

172
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:26,217
I'm sorry, but we weren't properly
introduced before we took our trip.

173
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:29,397
Hey, I'm freezing my goggles off,
and you're introducing yourself.

174
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:30,377
Let's get going.

175
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:32,540
Here, you can use one of these.

176
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:34,035
They're hand warmers.

177
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:35,710
Kari?

178
00:09:35,793 --> 00:09:36,623
Thanks a lot.

179
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:37,977
Boy, leave it to you.

180
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:39,460
Good old, reliable Joe.

181
00:09:40,100 --> 00:09:42,394
I watch all those survival shows on TV.

182
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:44,300
It won't open!

183
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:50,220
Joe, look!

184
00:09:50,780 --> 00:09:51,610
Huh?

185
00:09:51,693 --> 00:09:53,520
Whoa, go Mammon! Huh?

186
00:09:55,420 --> 00:09:56,250
Huh?

187
00:09:58,540 --> 00:10:00,000
Go, Mammon, speak to me.

188
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:01,730
Joe.

189
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:03,357
What day of the week is it?

190
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:04,960
It's Saturday. Actually,

191
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:08,337
it's Thursday, but you never did know
the day, so you're mad to your old self.

192
00:10:08,420 --> 00:10:10,077
I heard from Tentomon that we could use

193
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:12,497
that TV to contact you
if we were in trouble.

194
00:10:12,580 --> 00:10:15,277
Boy, it looks like you're gonna
wipe out my whole first aid kit.

195
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:17,900
I always get misty at happy reunions.

196
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:19,864
I actually think I'm gonna cry.

197
00:10:20,260 --> 00:10:21,090
Don't.

198
00:10:21,173 --> 00:10:22,003
Your tears will turn to icicles.

199
00:10:22,086 --> 00:10:23,980
You really look terrible, Gomamon.

200
00:10:24,640 --> 00:10:26,405
But I mean that in a nice way.

201
00:10:27,060 --> 00:10:30,413
I picked a fight with the
wrong guy, the Digimon Emperor.

202
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:36,400
He's built another control
spire here, too. What's that?

203
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:38,757
It's the Digimon Emperor's secret weapon.

204
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:41,677
He hunts down Digimon and puts
these dark rings around them,

205
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:43,017
turning them into his slaves.

206
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:46,037
And the control spires supply
the power to those rings.

207
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:47,680
And no one can Digivolve.

208
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:49,567
Dude, I'm gonna rip it down.

209
00:10:50,280 --> 00:10:52,217
But we're gonna have to cross this ice if

210
00:10:52,300 --> 00:10:54,817
we hope to get close
enough to destroy it now

211
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:56,317
I know what Matt means when he says I'm

212
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:59,200
walking on thin ice Did
you bring any skates?

213
00:10:59,400 --> 00:11:02,020
We need six pairs. Sorry. I'm all out.

214
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:03,160
Hey Joe.

215
00:11:03,460 --> 00:11:04,695
Do you have any rope?

216
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:21,500
Mm-hmm.

217
00:11:22,660 --> 00:11:23,490
Phew!

218
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:25,380
Well, that's done.

219
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:26,579
What a great sled.

220
00:11:26,780 --> 00:11:29,074
Now all we have to do is go for a ride.

221
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:30,748
That's easy for you to say.

222
00:11:30,860 --> 00:11:33,580
We're pulling. I'm no dog. Come on, guys.

223
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:34,737
We're counting on you.

224
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:35,650
Okay!

225
00:11:38,540 --> 00:11:39,500
Now mush!

226
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:40,990
Yay!

227
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:44,460
So they're here? Mm-hmm. Hmm?

228
00:11:48,580 --> 00:11:49,410
Gogemon!

229
00:11:49,493 --> 00:11:50,595
What a way to travel!

230
00:11:51,180 --> 00:11:52,010
Uh-oh!

231
00:11:52,093 --> 00:11:53,260
We've got visitors!

232
00:11:54,180 --> 00:11:56,160
Oh, look, snowmen! How cute!

233
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:59,853
No, they're Frigimon, but
what's that around their legs?

234
00:12:44,420 --> 00:12:45,437
We can outrun them.

235
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:46,350
What?

236
00:12:46,433 --> 00:12:48,237
Our mission is to destroy
the controls fire, right?

237
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:50,497
So it's better to keep going
than to waste time fighting.

238
00:12:50,580 --> 00:12:52,200
But they're attacking us!

239
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:53,908
Joe's right, run past them!

240
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:04,830
Oh, right!

241
00:13:04,913 --> 00:13:05,998
We made it through!

242
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:07,320
Aim for that hill!

243
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:13,460
They missed us by a mile!

244
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:19,060
Whoa, it's an alchemist!

245
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:42,180
I'll save him.

246
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,082
Warming up yet?

247
00:13:49,260 --> 00:13:50,417
Drink this herbal tea.

248
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:52,900
It's 10 % herbal and 90 % tea.

249
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:54,199
Thanks a lot, Joe.

250
00:13:54,420 --> 00:13:57,480
Boy, that Joe really comes
prepared. That's nothing.

251
00:13:57,700 --> 00:14:00,017
Wait until you see him
during hay fever season.

252
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:02,200
We'll have to leave Cody here. Mmm.

253
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:04,320
What? TK's right.

254
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:06,297
I'll stay back here and take care of Cody.

255
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:07,210
Thanks, Joe.

256
00:14:07,700 --> 00:14:09,340
I'm going too. Huh?

257
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:12,737
My grandfather told me if I rely
on myself and try my hardest,

258
00:14:12,820 --> 00:14:14,337
I won't let any of you down.

259
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:15,637
You're not letting us down.

260
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:18,177
And besides, you will need
to conserve your strength.

261
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:19,237
That's right, Cody.

262
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:21,777
We got a long fight ahead,
and we're gonna need you.

263
00:14:21,860 --> 00:14:23,095
I guess you're right.

264
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:25,040
I'll wait here.

265
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:26,358
Don't be gone long.

266
00:14:26,700 --> 00:14:29,935
We'll be back quicker than
you can say Digimon Emperor.

267
00:14:33,860 --> 00:14:34,820
Are you okay?

268
00:14:35,180 --> 00:14:37,020
A little tired. Me too.

269
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:39,197
I could really use a little nap.

270
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:42,157
I vote we take this opportunity
to get some shutout.

271
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:43,197
I couldn't sleep.

272
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:46,104
I feel I should be out
there helping the others.

273
00:14:46,220 --> 00:14:47,837
I know exactly what you're feeling.

274
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:50,077
I used to feel that way too,
but I thought it was nausea.

275
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:52,807
And then I slowly began
to realize something.

276
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:55,057
All of us are here for a reason.

277
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:58,777
There's a big picture that we can't see
yet, and I don't mean a widescreen TV.

278
00:14:58,860 --> 00:15:01,560
So us staying behind is for a reason.

279
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:03,150
But what?

280
00:15:05,060 --> 00:15:06,300
Come on, let's go!

281
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:15,720
Like my newest slave, Shellmon.

282
00:15:16,020 --> 00:15:20,380
His aqua blaster attack shoots water
so hard it can demolish solid rock.

283
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:23,856
It appears I've discovered
your secret little hideout.

284
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:26,630
Gomamon.

285
00:15:26,713 --> 00:15:28,997
Now I know the reason we
were supposed to stay behind.

286
00:15:29,080 --> 00:15:31,617
So the others can have the
time to destroy the spire.

287
00:15:31,700 --> 00:15:33,477
I need you to create a diversion.

288
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:36,037
Keep him busy with some of that
great Gomamon charm of yours.

289
00:15:36,120 --> 00:15:36,950
Gotcha.

290
00:15:37,160 --> 00:15:39,917
Why did one Shellmon take
the other Shellmon's lunch?

291
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,417
Because it was shellfish.

292
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:43,559
I guess you heard that one already.

293
00:15:44,460 --> 00:15:46,284
That's the great Gomamon charm?

294
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,037
Time to get down to business, B-Mom.

295
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:53,950
Let's do it.

296
00:15:58,520 --> 00:15:59,480
Digi-Armortize!

297
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:09,360
B-Mom, I'm a Digi-Bomb, too!

298
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:13,700
Digimon monsters, Digimon
are the champions!

299
00:16:16,620 --> 00:16:17,980
Armor! Digimon!

300
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:20,230
Digimon!

301
00:16:23,120 --> 00:16:26,200
Digimon monsters, Digimon
are the champions!

302
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:29,220
Fladramon, the fire of courage!

303
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:33,560
Fire rocket!

304
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:37,790
Help!

305
00:16:37,873 --> 00:16:38,703
You have no sense of humor!

306
00:16:38,786 --> 00:16:41,120
Try the knock-knock jokes.

307
00:16:41,480 --> 00:16:43,400
Are you ready? You bet.

308
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:49,140
Digi-Armor, energize!

309
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:56,340
Armadillo-Mon, Armored Digivolve, too.

310
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:03,110
Digma!

311
00:17:08,180 --> 00:17:10,480
Digma, the thrill of power!

312
00:17:11,120 --> 00:17:12,980
Armor, huh? Not bad!

313
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:17,520
Thanks, Digma! You're welcome!

314
00:17:17,980 --> 00:17:20,020
Hey, leave him alone!

315
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:22,140
Aqua Blasters! Cody!

316
00:17:27,340 --> 00:17:28,560
Don't worry, Cody.

317
00:17:28,820 --> 00:17:29,900
I'll protect you.

318
00:17:37,060 --> 00:17:39,600
Fladramon, the fire of courage.

319
00:17:41,140 --> 00:17:42,100
Strike three.

320
00:17:42,380 --> 00:17:44,637
Fladramon can handle
the Frigimon by himself,

321
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:46,797
so it's up to us to destroy the Spire.

322
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:49,557
Okay, but I think we're gonna
have to do it from the air.

323
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:50,470
Got it.

324
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:52,320
Hold on tight, Cody.

325
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:03,980
No problem.

326
00:18:04,420 --> 00:18:06,361
I'm never out of ideas or slaves.

327
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:11,049
Ebidramon here uses his twin scissors
attack to crush the enemy like a snail.

328
00:18:11,420 --> 00:18:13,440
Ebidramon, destroy them all!

329
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:18,130
Digmon!

330
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:23,137
If there was some way you
were able to digivolve,

331
00:18:23,220 --> 00:18:25,749
what's taking them so
long with that spire?

332
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:31,470
Star Shower!

333
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:34,830
Tempest Ring!

334
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:39,030
They did it!

335
00:18:39,113 --> 00:18:40,457
They destroyed the control spire!

336
00:18:40,540 --> 00:18:41,834
Now you can digivolve!

337
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:43,350
What?

338
00:18:43,433 --> 00:18:45,817
He said they destroyed the control
spire, now you can digivolve.

339
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:47,217
It's just a figure of speech!

340
00:18:47,300 --> 00:18:48,130
Digimon!

341
00:18:48,380 --> 00:18:49,210
Digimon!

342
00:18:49,620 --> 00:18:50,450
Digimon!

343
00:18:50,820 --> 00:18:52,600
Go on, Digimon!

344
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:57,000
Mikakumon!

345
00:19:03,940 --> 00:19:05,940
Now it's my turn!

346
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:07,680
Gold Rush!

347
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:11,117
You've got it!

348
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:12,417
Finish him, Mikakumon!

349
00:19:12,500 --> 00:19:13,441
Harpoon torpedo!

350
00:19:20,820 --> 00:19:23,526
All right, Gabumon,
you're in charge here now.

351
00:19:23,640 --> 00:19:26,457
Great, a frozen wasteland,
just what I always wanted.

352
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:29,157
At least you'll have plenty of
time to practice your jokes.

353
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:30,080
Very funny.

354
00:19:30,360 --> 00:19:32,357
I guess we'd better be heading back home.

355
00:19:32,440 --> 00:19:35,157
Before we go, there's one
thing I just have to finish.

356
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:36,070
Oh, really?

357
00:19:36,153 --> 00:19:36,983
What's that?

358
00:19:37,066 --> 00:19:37,896
Our introduction.

359
00:19:38,240 --> 00:19:39,680
Hello, my name's Cody.

360
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:42,137
I don't get it, Cody.

361
00:19:42,220 --> 00:19:43,050
What's the big deal?

362
00:19:43,133 --> 00:19:45,337
My grandfather says that
next to prune juice,

363
00:19:45,420 --> 00:19:48,077
manners are the most important
thing a man can have.

364
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:50,857
You know, Cody reminds
me an awful lot of Joe.

365
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:53,017
Always honest and sticks to the rules.

366
00:19:53,100 --> 00:19:54,865
I think he reminds me of Izzy.

367
00:19:54,980 --> 00:19:56,660
Just loaded with curiosity.

368
00:19:57,340 --> 00:19:58,800
Part Izzy and part me?

369
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,557
That's a scary combination.

370
00:20:00,640 --> 00:20:02,346
He's got a split personality.

371
00:20:03,760 --> 00:20:04,590
Blast!

372
00:20:04,673 --> 00:20:06,237
They've destroyed another control spire.

373
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:08,757
And that was a freshly
conquered area, too.

374
00:20:08,840 --> 00:20:09,717
All right, then.

375
00:20:09,800 --> 00:20:11,624
I'll just have to go to plan B.

376
00:20:12,160 --> 00:20:13,807
Hey, Wormon, what is plan B?

377
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:17,110
Well?

378
00:20:17,193 --> 00:20:18,509
We can all become friends.

379
00:20:19,380 --> 00:20:21,027
That's not plan B, you fool!

380
00:20:21,240 --> 00:20:23,005
Don't blame me, I can't spell.

381
00:20:25,240 --> 00:20:26,660
I bet he's home crying.

382
00:20:26,940 --> 00:20:30,116
Mommy, those mean kids broke
another one of my spires.

383
00:20:30,920 --> 00:20:32,620
The fight's not over yet.

384
00:20:33,120 --> 00:20:35,257
Joe, will you come back
and fight with us again?

385
00:20:35,340 --> 00:20:36,380
Sure, who knows?

386
00:20:36,560 --> 00:20:38,817
Maybe I'll even find the
digi-egg of my own someday.

387
00:20:38,900 --> 00:20:40,057
But I have to watch my cholesterol.

388
00:20:40,140 --> 00:20:42,337
i was wondering if you'd
like to come over to my house

389
00:20:42,420 --> 00:20:44,737
sometime i think you'd like
my grandfather and i know

390
00:20:44,820 --> 00:20:47,557
he'd like you sure i love
prune juice is it okay if i

391
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:49,897
come over too i would just
love meeting your grandfather

392
00:20:49,980 --> 00:20:52,637
if carrie's going i'm going
too you always have to

393
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:55,497
do everything i do but you
and i are partners sorry

394
00:20:55,580 --> 00:20:59,897
davis but you already have
a partner uh you mean him

395
00:20:59,980 --> 00:21:04,020
yeah you got a problem with
that it's just not the same

396
00:22:07,360 --> 00:22:09,860
I don't know.
